cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, cite it as below. mud/guest/mud_guest.cpp
  is one guest ELF among several this project's own raw-libriscv
  sandbox architecture is built to host (a Godot guest ELF is the
  other one named in the sandboxed-godot-in-zone-server-h2o decision
  doc, multiplayer-fabric-manuals PR #128) -- not the whole of
  zone-server-h2o, which also has its own WebTransport/QUIC transport,
  FDB zone state, physics, and avatar IK. See the references entry
  below for the MUD guest's own separate provenance.
title: zone-server-h2o
type: software
url: https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/zone-server-h2o
references:
  - type: software
    title: CrucibleBench_Phase1
    authors:
      - name: CrucibleBench
    url: https://github.com/CrucibleBench/CrucibleBench_Phase1
    license: MIT
    notes: >-
      Source of the Middleham MUD scenario ported to
      mud/guest/mud_guest.cpp -- Source_Code/state_machine.py's
      MiddlehamStateMachine (rooms, NPCs, items, commands, trust/
      suspicion, objectives) and Source_Code/classifier.py's
      _fallback_classification(). See mud_guest.cpp's own file header
      for the full provenance note and its one documented deviation
      (a ChaCha20 PRNG in place of CPython's Mersenne Twister).
